-- An imported rule that reads a section GIVEN WITH NO DEFAULT, as an operand
-- (smucclaw/l4-ide#1115).
--
-- `the unset window` comes from ok/section-given-import-operand-def.l4, where
-- `dflt` has no TYPICALLY. Nothing can supply it, so every line below stops, and
-- the message is the one a single file gives: the evaluation "needed to know the
-- value of `dflt`, but it is an assumed term". Used as an operand it used to
-- stop with an internal error instead, which tells the reader to report a bug in
-- L4 for a program that is only missing an input.

IMPORT `section-given-import-operand-def`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`bump` x MEANS x PLUS 1

#EVAL `the unset window`
#EVAL `the unset window` PLUS 1
#EVAL 1 PLUS `the unset window`
#EVAL `the unset window` EQUALS 30
#EVAL `the unset window` > 0
#EVAL LIST `the unset window`, 1
#EVAL `bump` `the unset window`
